    <TD>&nbsp;</TD>
    <TD STYLE="padding-top: 0.25pt; padding-right: 0.25pt; padding-left: 0.25pt; text-align: left"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Each Placement Agent Warrant will be exercisable to purchase one ADS.
Each Placement Agent Warrant will have an initial exercise price of $1.30 per ADS, will be exercisable upon issuance, and will expire
five (5) years from the commencement of sales of the offering. The Placement Agent Warrants are in substantially the same form as the
Series A Warrants except the cashless exercise provision to which holders of Placement Agent Warrants have the option to exercise and
for no additional cash consideration and receive an aggregate number of ADSs equal to the product of&nbsp;&nbsp;(i) the aggregate number
of Placement Agent Warrant ADSs that would be issuable upon exercise of the Placement Agent Warrant in accordance with the terms of this
Placement Agent Warrant if such exercise were by means of a cash exercise rather than a cashless exercise, multiplied by (ii) 2.0. Accordingly,
we believe it is highly unlikely that a holder of the Placement Agent Warrants would pay an exercise price in cash to receive one ADS
when the holder could instead choose the zero cash exercise option and pay no cash to receive more ADSs than they would receive if they
did pay an exercise price. As a result, we will likely not receive any additional funds and do not expect to receive any additional funds
upon the exercise of the Placement Agent Warrants.</FONT></TD></TR>
  <TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">
    <TD STYLE="padding-top: 0.25pt; padding-right: 0.25pt; padding-left: 0.25pt; text-align: left">&nbsp;</TD>
